<title>GREECE: Greek retail sales rise 6.7 pct yr/yr in June.</title>
<headline>Greek retail sales rise 6.7 pct yr/yr in June.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek retail sales rose 6.7 percent year-on-year in June after rising 16.7 percent in May, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said in a statement.</p>
<p>Foodstuffs rose by 4.8 percent, apparel and footwear by 2.2 percent, furniture and household goods by 13.8 percent and miscellaneous goods by 7.9 percent, it said.</p>
<p>On average, retail sales rose 10.5 percent in the period January-June 1996 compared to the same period a year ago, NSS said.  </p>
<p>    RETAIL SALES	   June 96   May 96   June 95</p>
<p>    Year-on-year (pct)     6.7%     16.7%	3.6%</p>
<p>    Index (1988=100)     251.3     257.1     235.4</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
